// Permit SellShares only when the recorded result settles to zero proceeds.
// The new idea: `context.output` is *optional* (it exists only after the tool
// resolves), so we guard the read with `context has output`, and we compare
// the `proceeds` decimal with `==` since decimals support equality only.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"SellShares",
    resource
)
when {
    if context has output
    then context.output.proceeds == decimal("0.0")
    else false
};
